# Continuum compatibility, values, disconnect and replay, inert intents

## Goal

Carry continuum values between a simulated edge and a simulated cloud host
over the Lab's bounded in-memory channel: a manifest is admitted only when it
is compatible, an intent that arrives before any manifest is inert, a
duplicated intent dispatches once, reordered and dropped proposals never move
the observed state backwards, a disconnection replays unacknowledged
deliveries without a second mutation, and capacity is bounded. The checked-in
fixture is the canonical manifest bytes produced by the continuum codec.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"}
])
```

The requirement above is a published-artifact requirement. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`priv/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout. No network is used;
the channel and both endpoints live in this VM.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Value kinds, canonical codec, compatibility, lifecycle | `wotex_continuum` (package-implements) | `WotexContinuum.Codec`, `Manifest`, `Compatibility`, `Lifecycle` |
| Action dispatch on the cloud side | `wotex_runtime` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Runtime.ConsumedThing.invoke_action/4` |
| Channel, delivery records, fault schedule, disconnect and replay | `wotex_lab` (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.Continuum.Channel`, `FaultSchedule` |
| Admission, watermarks, at-most-once dispatch, remote context | `wotex_lab` host (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.Continuum.Host` |
| Wire conversions from Nx and runtime values | `wotex_lab` (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.Continuum.Wire` |

Continuum intent is owned by the consumer host: the package defines the
value; the Lab host decides whether an intent is executed, once, or refused.

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Lab
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Runtime.{Loopback, StaticRef}
alias Wotex.Lab.Continuum.{Channel, FaultSchedule, Host, Wire}
alias Wotex.Lab.Reference.Thing
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
alias Wotex.Nx.Observation
alias Wotex.Runtime.{BindingProfile, ConsumedThing}
alias Wotex.ThingDescription

alias WotexContinuum.{
  ActionIntent,
  ActionResult,
  Capability,
  Codec,
  Compatibility,
  Delivery,
  ExecutionScope,
  Lifecycle,
  Manifest,
  Mode
}

telemetry_id = "cookbook-continuum-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception, :measurement],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())
epoch = ~U[2026-09-08 10:00:00Z]
clock = fn -> epoch end
```

The fixture manifest decodes through the public codec; the host's capability
satisfies the manifest's compatibility requirement.

```elixir
fixture_dir = Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/continuum")
{:ok, manifest} = fixture_dir |> Path.join("continuum-manifest.json") |> File.read!() |> Codec.decode()
{:ok, expected} = fixture_dir |> Path.join("expected-output.json") |> File.read!() |> Wotex.JSON.decode()

{:ok, capability} =
  Capability.from_map(%{
    id: "observation-forwarding",
    version: "2.1.0",
    operations: ["forward"],
    modes: [:hybrid, :saas],
    network: :external,
    degradation: :queue
  })

{:ok, mode} = Mode.from_map(%{deployment: :hybrid, connectivity: :connected})

scope = fn node_id ->
  {:ok, scope} =
    ExecutionScope.from_map(%{execution_id: "exec-1", node_id: node_id, mode: mode, observed_at: epoch})

  scope
end

{manifest.manifest_id, Manifest.compatible_with?(manifest, WotexContinuum.schema_version(), [capability])}
```

The cloud side owns a consumed loopback Thing; the edge is this process.
Each channel is started with an explicit fault schedule and clock, and a host
attaches to its `cloud` endpoint.

```elixir
{:ok, lab} = Lab.start_link(id: "continuum", max_children: 32)
{:ok, td} = Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/loopback/thing-description.json") |> File.read!() |> ThingDescription.parse()
thing_id = ThingDescription.id(td)

{:ok, thing} =
  Lab.start_child(
    lab,
    :things,
    {Thing, td: td, state: %{"temperature" => 20.0, "target" => 21.0}, tokens: %{"bearer_sc" => "room-token"}}
  )

{:ok, profile} = BindingProfile.new(id: :loopback, schemes: ["loopback"], operations: Wotex.Runtime.operations())

{:ok, consumed} =
  ConsumedThing.new(td,
    profiles: [profile],
    transports: %{loopback: {Loopback, %{host: thing}}},
    credentials: {StaticRef, %{references: %{"bearer_sc" => "ref"}, lookup: fn "ref" -> {:ok, "room-token"} end}}
  )

pair = fn id, faults ->
  {:ok, channel} =
    Lab.start_child(lab, :sessions, {Channel, id: id, clock: clock, capacity: 8, faults: faults})

  {:ok, host} =
    Lab.start_child(
      lab,
      :sessions,
      {Host,
       id: {:host, id},
       channel: channel,
       endpoint: "cloud",
       clock: clock,
       things: %{thing_id => consumed},
       capabilities: [capability]}
    )

  :ok = Channel.attach(channel, "edge-a", self())
  {channel, host}
end

wait_until = fn read, predicate ->
  Enum.reduce_while(1..200, read.(), fn _attempt, value ->
    if predicate.(value), do: {:halt, value}, else: (Process.sleep(5) && {:cont, read.()})
  end)
end

{:ok, intent} =
  ActionIntent.from_map(%{
    intent_id: "intent-1",
    thing_id: thing_id,
    action_name: "setTarget",
    input: 22.0,
    requested_at: epoch,
    idempotency_key: "set-22",
    context: scope.("edge-a")
  })

{:ok, faults} = FaultSchedule.new(duplicate: [2])
FaultSchedule.version()
```

Compatibility gates intents. Before any manifest, an intent is recorded and
refused as stale authority; an incompatible manifest is refused; the fixture
manifest is admitted.

```elixir
{plain, plain_host} = pair.(:plain, [])

{:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(plain, "edge-a", "cloud", intent)
stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(plain_host) end, &(length(&1.rejected) == 1))
[%{reason: before_manifest}] = stats.rejected
calls_before = Thing.stats(thing).handler_calls

{:ok, incompatible_requirement} =
  Compatibility.from_map(%{
    schema_requirement: "~> 2.0",
    required_capabilities: [%{id: "observation-forwarding", version_requirement: ">= 9.0.0"}]
  })

{:ok, incompatible} =
  Manifest.from_map(%{
    manifest_id: "manifest-old",
    artifact: %{name: "edge-worker", version: "0.0.1", digest: "sha256:" <> String.duplicate("b", 64)},
    compatibility: incompatible_requirement,
    supported_modes: [:hybrid],
    capabilities: []
  })

{:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(plain, "edge-a", "cloud", incompatible)
stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(plain_host) end, &(length(&1.rejected) == 2))
incompatible_reason = stats.rejected |> List.last() |> Map.fetch!(:reason)

{:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(plain, "edge-a", "cloud", manifest)
stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(plain_host) end, &(&1.manifests == ["manifest-edge-a"]))
{before_manifest, calls_before, incompatible_reason, stats.manifests}
```

A duplicated delivery of the intent (fault schedule: sequence 2 twice)
dispatches once; the result crosses back to the edge as an `action_result`.

```elixir
{dup, dup_host} = pair.(:duplicate, duplicate: [2])
{:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(dup, "edge-a", "cloud", manifest)
{:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(dup, "edge-a", "cloud", intent)
stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(dup_host) end, &(length(&1.received) == 3))

result =
  receive do
    {:wotex_continuum, "edge-a", delivery_id, wire} ->
      :ok = Channel.ack(dup, delivery_id)
      {:ok, %ActionResult{} = decoded} = Codec.decode(wire)
      decoded
  after
    2_000 -> :no_result
  end

dup_dispatches = stats.dispatches
dup_calls = Thing.stats(thing).handler_calls
{dup_dispatches, Enum.map(stats.rejected, & &1.reason), dup_calls, result.status}
```

Reordering and loss: sequence 3 is held until sequence 4 is sent, and
sequence 5 is dropped. The watermark keeps the observed value at the highest
admitted sequence.

```elixir
{ordered, ordered_host} = pair.(:ordered, hold: %{3 => 4}, drop: [5])
{:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(ordered, "edge-a", "cloud", manifest)

proposal = fn sequence, value ->
  {:ok, observation} =
    Observation.new(
      id: "obs-#{sequence}",
      thing_id: thing_id,
      affordance_type: :property,
      affordance_name: "temperature",
      observed_at: sequence * 1_000,
      value: value,
      unit: "Cel"
    )

  {:ok, proposal} = Wire.proposal_from_observation(observation, scope.("edge-a"), epoch, sequence: sequence)
  proposal
end

for {sequence, value} <- [{1, 20.0}, {2, 21.0}, {3, 22.0}] do
  {:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(ordered, "edge-a", "cloud", proposal.(sequence, value))
end

stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(ordered_host) end, &(length(&1.received) == 4))
observed = stats.observations[{thing_id, :property, "temperature"}]
{:ok, %Delivery{status: dropped_status, error: dropped_error}} = Channel.send_value(ordered, "edge-a", "cloud", proposal.(4, 30.0))
after_drop = Host.stats(ordered_host).observations[{thing_id, :property, "temperature"}]

{Enum.map(stats.received, & &1.item_id), Enum.map(stats.rejected, & &1.reason), observed.sequence, dropped_status, dropped_error, after_drop.sequence}
```

Disconnect and replay: a silent endpoint never acknowledges, so the delivery
stays in flight; a disconnected channel buffers new sends as `pending`, and a
reconnect replays both with a new attempt. The same replay against a real
host produces one dispatch.

```elixir
{:ok, silent_channel} = Lab.start_child(lab, :sessions, {Channel, id: :silent, clock: clock})
:ok = Channel.attach(silent_channel, "edge-a", self())
:ok = Channel.attach(silent_channel, "silent", self())
{:ok, first} = Channel.send_value(silent_channel, "edge-a", "silent", manifest)

first_seen =
  receive do
    {:wotex_continuum, "silent", id, _wire} -> id
  after
    500 -> :nothing
  end

:ok = Channel.disconnect(silent_channel)
{:ok, buffered} = Channel.send_value(silent_channel, "edge-a", "silent", capability)

while_disconnected =
  receive do
    {:wotex_continuum, "silent", _id, _wire} -> :delivered
  after
    50 -> :nothing
  end

:ok = Channel.reconnect(silent_channel)

replayed =
  for _copy <- 1..2 do
    receive do
      {:wotex_continuum, "silent", id, _wire} -> id
    after
      500 -> :nothing
    end
  end

attempts = silent_channel |> Channel.deliveries() |> Enum.map(& &1.attempt)

{replay, replay_host} = pair.(:replay, [])
:ok = Channel.disconnect(replay)
{:ok, _manifest} = Channel.send_value(replay, "edge-a", "cloud", manifest)
{:ok, _intent} = Channel.send_value(replay, "edge-a", "cloud", intent)
:ok = Channel.reconnect(replay)
replay_stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(replay_host) end, &(map_size(&1.dispatches) == 1))

{first.delivery_id == first_seen, buffered.status, while_disconnected, Enum.sort(replayed) == Enum.sort([first.delivery_id, buffered.delivery_id]), attempts, replay_stats.dispatches}
```

## Deliberate breakage

Capacity is the number of unacknowledged deliveries; the third send on a
capacity-two channel is refused. A draining host refuses intents, and an
unregistered value is refused by the channel before encoding.

```elixir
{:ok, bounded} = Lab.start_child(lab, :sessions, {Channel, id: :bounded, clock: clock, capacity: 2})
:ok = Channel.attach(bounded, "edge-a", self())
:ok = Channel.attach(bounded, "silent", self())
{:ok, _one} = Channel.send_value(bounded, "edge-a", "silent", mode)
{:ok, _two} = Channel.send_value(bounded, "edge-a", "silent", mode)
{:error, %Wotex.Lab.Error{code: capacity_code, class: capacity_class}} = Channel.send_value(bounded, "edge-a", "silent", mode)

{:ok, %Lifecycle{state: draining_state}} = Host.drain(plain_host)
{:ok, _delivery} = Channel.send_value(plain, "edge-a", "cloud", intent)
plain_stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(plain_host) end, &(length(&1.rejected) == 3))
draining_reason = plain_stats.rejected |> List.last() |> Map.fetch!(:reason)

{:error, %Wotex.Lab.Error{code: unregistered_code}} = Channel.send_value(plain, "edge-a", "cloud", %{"kind" => "x"})
{capacity_code, capacity_class, draining_state, draining_reason, unregistered_code}
```

```elixir
:ok = Supervisor.stop(lab)
```

## Safe telemetry

Codec spans label the operation and the value kind; byte counts are
measurements. Thing ids, inputs and wire bytes never become labels.

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)

kinds =
  for {[:wotex, :lab, :continuum, :codec, :measurement], %{bytes: bytes}, %{kind: kind}} <- spans,
      do: {kind, bytes}

text = inspect(spans)
labels_safe? = kinds != [] and not (text =~ thing_id) and not (text =~ "22.0")
{kinds |> Enum.map(&elem(&1, 0)) |> Enum.uniq(), labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `manifest-compatible` | The fixture manifest is compatible and admitted as `manifest-edge-a` |
| `manifest-incompatible` | A `>= 9.0.0` requirement is refused as `:incompatible_manifest` |
| `intent-without-manifest-inert` | The early intent is `:stale_authority` and the Thing handler was never called |
| `duplicate-intent-once` | One dispatch, one `:duplicate_intent` refusal, one handler call, an `:accepted` result |
| `reordered-proposal-stale` | Received order `obs-1, obs-3, obs-2`; `obs-2` is `:stale_observation`; watermark 3 |
| `dropped-delivery` | Sequence 5 is `failed` with error `dropped` and the watermark stays 3 |
| `replay-after-reconnect` | Both deliveries replay with attempts `[2, 1]`; the real host dispatches once |
| `capacity-bounded` | The third unacknowledged send is `:capacity_exhausted`, class `:unavailable` |

```elixir
vectors = expected["vectors"]

%{
  "manifest-compatible" =>
    Manifest.compatible_with?(manifest, WotexContinuum.schema_version(), [capability]) == :ok and
      stats.manifests == ["manifest-edge-a"] and
      manifest.manifest_id == vectors["continuum:manifest-compatible"]["manifest_id"],
  "manifest-incompatible" => incompatible_reason == :incompatible_manifest,
  "intent-without-manifest-inert" => before_manifest == :stale_authority and calls_before == 0,
  "duplicate-intent-once" =>
    match?(%{"set-22" => %{duplicates: 1, outcome: {:ok, :accepted}}}, dup_dispatches) and
      result.status == :accepted and dup_calls == 1,
  "reordered-proposal-stale" =>
    Enum.map(stats.received, & &1.item_id) == ["manifest-edge-a", "obs-1", "obs-3", "obs-2"] and
      Enum.map(stats.rejected, & &1.reason) == [:stale_observation] and observed.sequence == 3,
  "dropped-delivery" => dropped_status == :failed and dropped_error.code == "dropped" and after_drop.sequence == 3,
  "replay-after-reconnect" =>
    buffered.status == :pending and while_disconnected == :nothing and attempts == [2, 1] and
      match?(%{"set-22" => %{duplicates: 0}}, replay_stats.dispatches),
  "capacity-bounded" =>
    capacity_code == :capacity_exhausted and capacity_class == :unavailable and
      draining_reason == :host_not_accepting and unregistered_code == :invalid_continuum_value and
      labels_safe?
}
```

## Public seam

`lab.continuum_channel` is Lab-owned: the package defines values and the
codec, and the Lab channel and host implement transport, admission and
at-most-once dispatch. The runtime seam `runtime.transport` carries the
dispatched Action.

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.05 (`WLB-C05`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream consumer evidence: `WCT-C01`, `WCT-C02`, `WCT-C03`, `WCT-C04`.

## Replacement adapter

Replace the in-memory channel with a real transport that delivers the
canonical bytes from `WotexContinuum.Codec.encode/2` and reports the same
`WotexContinuum.Delivery` states. Keep the host's rules: no intent without an
admitted manifest, one dispatch per idempotency key, and a watermark per
affordance. Nothing in the package or the channel grants execution; the host
does, once.
